WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.700
- [Narrator] There is nothing
as obnoxious as some jerk

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.760
laying on their horn in traffic.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.190
Although it's something
that we all love to hate,

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.720
the horn does in fact have a purpose.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.433
Because before, it was madness.

00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:15.266
- [Man] Learn to drive.

00:00:15.266 --> 00:00:16.683
- [Man] Get outta here.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.370
- [Woman] Get out of my way.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.565
- [Woman] Oh, you dingbat.

00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:22.750
- [Narrator] In the early
days of the automobile,

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.800
the roads were a riot of sound.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.490
Drivers could use
whistles, sirens and bells

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.840
to alert pedestrians and other
cars what they were up to.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.400
If you were driving in London,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.020
every car had to have
a guy with a red flag

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:35.920
walk in front of it.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.363
Imagine being that guy.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.630
Miller Reese Hutchison was an inventor

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.270
who lived in New York City.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.780
Disturbed by the increasing
number of accidents,

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.521
he sat down and invented the klaxon,

00:00:48.521 --> 00:00:51.531
which was a horn with a
sound so unique and distinct,

00:00:51.531 --> 00:00:55.943
it became the preferred choice
for cars and their drivers.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.609
The invention delighted the
people of the UK so much

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:05.150
a car race called the
Emancipation Run was created

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.600
to celebrate getting rid of that flag guy

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.710
and replacing him with a horn.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.890
It runs to this day.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.960
Miller Reese Hutchison went
on to many great things.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.720
He worked for Thomas Edison.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.890
He also invented the
first practical version

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.170
of the hearing aid.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.520
But the car horn is perhaps
his most iconic creation.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.260
Love them or hate them, it
changed the acoustic landscape

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.610
of the world and gave you
a way to give that guy

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.283
who just cut you off a piece of your mind.

